# profile_pocket_clear_rough.cam — the prismatic roughing fixture: profile_pocket_clear.cam plus a
# stock_to_leave allowance (DECISIONS.md "stock_to_leave is a radial
# allowance…"). The finishing sibling is profile_pocket_clear.cam; the two differ by exactly
# the field, so the goldens diff as the skin and nothing else.
#
# The allowance is RADIAL. On a pocket the wall is the only surface defined by
# geometry — the floor is the feature's own `extent`, an authored number the
# allowance never moves — so the whole 0.5mm becomes radial offset and the cusp
# budget is structurally 0.000: every loop sits at one Z, so no adjacent pair
# leaves a cusp, and validate() requires a flat-bottomed tool, so there is no
# floor scallop either.
#
# Hand-checked anchors (60mm square from 20 to 80, T5 dia 10 so r = 5,
# stepover 4, skin 0.5):
#   - the spiral starts at r + skin = 5.5 from the boundary, so the OUTERMOST
#     loop (emitted last — pocket machines innermost-out) runs 25.5 .. 74.5,
#     against profile_pocket_clear.cam's 25 .. 75. That 0.5 is the wall skin.
#   - offsets run 5.5, 9.5, ... 29.5; 33.5 exceeds the 30mm inradius and prunes
#     empty, so the INNERMOST loop (emitted first, with the ramp) is at 29.5:
#     49.5 .. 50.5, against profile_pocket_clear.cam's 49 .. 51.
#   - last pass reaches 29.5 + 5 = 34.5 >= the 30mm inradius, so no uncut
#     island stands at the centre.
#   - the floor is untouched at Z-5.000: `extent` is the depth, and a radial
#     allowance has no business moving it.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature PocketProfile ProfilePocket(extent=5.0
    20 20
    80 20
    80 80
    20 80
)

run Clear(tool=T5, profile=PocketProfile, stepover=4.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
